Unix utility 'free'

The 'free' Unix utility is responsible for displaying installed, reserved and in use memory of the
system, in kilobytes:

 total     - all the memory of the computer.
 wired     - memory held by the kernel, which cannot be given to anyone else.
 processes - memory held by running processes.
 free      - memory not in use.

USAGE:

free

No additional parameters are required.

For more information, enter 'free ?' or 'free --help'.

HISTORY

This command appeared in the Hexagonix H1 or in previous development versions (2015-2021).

